bpf: programs on tracepoints for l4h, without kprobes or uprobes

BPF_EVENTS, which BPF programs on tracepoints, kprobes and uprobes need,
also needs kprobe or uprobe events, which l4h has neither of (no int3
patching, no uprobes).  Android's bpfloader loads programs on
tracepoints (gpu_mem, sched, power, vmscan), and system_server stops when
the maps they would fill are missing.  With l4h, event tracing is enough.

--- a/kernel/trace/Kconfig
+++ b/kernel/trace/Kconfig
@@ -809,7 +809,7 @@
 
 config BPF_EVENTS
 	depends on BPF_SYSCALL
-	depends on (KPROBE_EVENTS || UPROBE_EVENTS) && PERF_EVENTS
+	depends on (KPROBE_EVENTS || UPROBE_EVENTS || (L4H && EVENT_TRACING)) && PERF_EVENTS
 	bool
 	default y
 	help
